{"name":"Hacienda White","hex":"#f0ede7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hacienda","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large homestead in a ranch or estate, usually in places where Colonial Spanish culture has had architectural influence."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hacienda"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hacienda","blocks":[{"text":"A hacienda is an estate, similar to a Roman latifundium, in Spain and the former Spanish Empire. With origins in Andalusia, haciendas were variously plantations, mines or factories, with many haciendas combining these activities. The word is derived from Spanish hacer and haciendo (making), referring to productive business enterprises."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Hacienda_Lealtad%2C_former_coffee_plantation_in_Lares%2C_Puerto_Rico_03.jpg/330px-Hacienda_Lealtad%2C_former_coffee_plantation_in_Lares%2C_Puerto_Rico_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hacienda","wikidata":"Q917730"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Hacienda_of_Xcanchakan%281843%29.jpg/500px-Hacienda_of_Xcanchakan%281843%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Hacienda_of_Xcanchakan%281843%29.jpg/500px-Hacienda_of_Xcanchakan%281843%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hacienda of Xcanchakan, Yucatán, Mexico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHacienda_of_Xcanchakan(1843).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Teatro_de_Atequiza%2C_Mexico.JPG/500px-Teatro_de_Atequiza%2C_Mexico.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Teatro_de_Atequiza%2C_Mexico.JPG/500px-Teatro_de_Atequiza%2C_Mexico.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wheat mill and theatre of Vicente Gallardo; Hacienda Atequiza, Jalisco, Mexico, 1886.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATeatro_de_Atequiza%2C_Mexico.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Hacendado_Propri%C3%A9taire_by_Claudio_Linati_1828.jpg/500px-Hacendado_Propri%C3%A9taire_by_Claudio_Linati_1828.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Hacendado_Propri%C3%A9taire_by_Claudio_Linati_1828.jpg/1280px-Hacendado_Propri%C3%A9taire_by_Claudio_Linati_1828.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wiki